From d80dcf9e6d4c9996dedbe596ca82e33e7fb9c567 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glib Shpychka <23005347+gshpychka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:00:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sessions): let a tool result follow its question's typed
 answer

A turn that asks a question records the typed answer it admits in its own
async context, but the validation of the turn's tool and assistant appends
runs in the session metadata worker, which cannot read that context. The
answer then counted as an unrelated newer user turn, the tool result was
refused, and the turn failed.

The turn now resolves its admitted answers when it prepares an append and
passes them to the validation, on the main thread and in the worker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNTt5yXBj4uDUwJmPGvXLd
